# The same daemon under its previous name. Two of them would own one fan, which
# is the arrangement this project exists to prevent, so dpkg is told to refuse
# rather than left to allow it.
Conflicts: ombra
Replaces: ombra
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: thermal, noise and backlight daemon for the ASUS Zenbook 14 UX3405MA
 A daemon that keeps an ASUS Zenbook 14 UX3405MA (Intel Core Ultra 9 185H)
 inside a chosen thermal envelope, and a tray console to switch between
 envelopes and to tune them by ear.
 .
 The firmware on this machine exposes no fan control and its performance
 profile removes the power limit entirely, so the only way to influence
 temperature and noise is to control how much heat the package produces. This
 daemon does that from static per-mode setpoints, records one telemetry sample
 per second so the setpoints can be tuned from data, and keeps an emergency
 thermal guard active regardless of mode.
 .
 It also follows the ambient light sensor to adjust display brightness around
 the level the person set, which is a separate function with its own profile
 and switch: selecting a thermal mode never moves the backlight.
 .
 The controls it writes exist only on this hardware. It is the sole owner of
 them, so it replaces the vendor daemon rather than layering on top of it.
